Ibex licensing
==============

Ibex is a derivative work of HAProxy (https://www.haproxy.org/), and inherits
HAProxy's licensing split. HAProxy deliberately applies the LGPL to its
exportable library code and the GPL to everything else; Ibex keeps that
boundary at the same place.

  crates/ebtree        LGPL-2.1-only        -> LICENSE.LGPL-2.1
  everything else      GPL-2.0-or-later     -> LICENSE.GPL-2.0

Why the two differ
------------------

The ebtree implementation is a port of Willy Tarreau's elastic binary trees
(haproxy include/import/ebtree*.h, src/eb*.c), whose headers read:

    This library is free software; you can redistribute it and/or
    modify it under the terms of the GNU Lesser General Public
    License as published by the Free Software Foundation, version 2.1
    exclusively.

Note "exclusively": that grant is version 2.1 only, with no "or later"
option, so the correct SPDX identifier is LGPL-2.1-only and the crate may
not be relicensed to LGPL-3.0.

The remaining crates port HAProxy core sources such as src/task.c, whose
headers read:

    This program is free software; you can redistribute it and/or
    modify it under the terms of the GNU General Public License
    as published by the Free Software Foundation; either version
    2 of the License, or (at your option) any later version.

That grant does carry the "or later" option, hence GPL-2.0-or-later.

Copyright
---------

Portions derived from HAProxy are Copyright 2000-2026 Willy Tarreau and the
HAProxy contributors. Each ported file carries an SPDX identifier and an
attribution header naming the specific upstream file it derives from.
